Load the OnePlus 6's speaker amplifier driver (snd_soc_max98927). The port's module list is the OnePlus 6T's, whose
speaker amplifier is a TFA98xx; the OnePlus 6's device tree has a Maxim MAX98927 (i2c 0x3a) on the speaker DAI
link instead. Without its driver the sound card (sdm845-sndcard) waits for that codec forever (devices_deferred:
soc@0:sound) and the phone has no sound card at all. With it, card 0 "sdm845 - OnePlus 6" registers with its
PCM devices. (OH's audio stack still needs to be set up for this card; audio_server stays stopped at boot.)

diff --git a/fajita/modules/modules.load b/fajita/modules/modules.load
index ae0af72..8392b93 100644
--- a/fajita/modules/modules.load
+++ b/fajita/modules/modules.load
@@ -38,6 +38,7 @@ ecdh_generic
 mc
 soundwire_bus
 snd_soc_tfa98xx
+snd_soc_max98927
 videodev
 snd_soc_rl6231
 videobuf2_common
